<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Donaueschingen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Donaueschingen is a town in the Black Forest-Baar district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, at the meeting of the Brigach and Breg, which form the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>. From the 18th century it was the residence of the princes of Fürstenberg, whose palace park contains a spring regarded as the source of the Danube. The town has held a festival of contemporary music since 1921.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/donaueschingen.jpg" alt="Donaueschingen" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JoachimKohler-HB · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Donaueschingen_Lammplatz_und_Stadtkirche_(2025).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
